  "output": "We are given: \"John buys twice as many red ties as blue ties. The red ties cost 50% more than blue ties. He spent $200 on blue ties that cost $40 each. How much did he spend on ties?\"\n\nLet's parse:\n- Blue ties cost $40 each.\n- He spent $200 on blue ties. So number of blue ties = 200 / 40 = 5 ties.\n- Red ties cost 50% more than blue ties. So red tie cost = 40 + 50% of 40 = 40 + 20 = $60 each.\n- He buys twice as many red ties as blue ties. So number of red ties = 2 * (number of blue ties) = 2 * 5 = 10 ties.\n- Total spent on ties = cost of blue ties + cost of red ties = 200 + (10 * 60) = 200 + 600 = $800.\n\nSo answer is 800.\n\nCheck: Blue: 5 ties * $40 = $200. Red: 10 ties * $60 = $600. Total $800.\n\nThus final answer: 800.</think>John spends $200 on blue ties at $40 each, so he buys 5 blue ties. Red ties cost 50% more than blue ties, so they cost $60 each. He buys twice as many red ties as blue ties, so he buys 10 red ties. Total spending is $200 + (10 × $60) = $200 + $600 = $800.\n\nFINAL: 800",
